# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
from lib import *
G = 'notice'

page('ad-account-disabled-circumventing-systems-help', G,
 'Ad Account Disabled for Circumventing Systems: Help',
 'Ad account disabled for circumventing systems? What Meta means by it, what to check before you appeal, and how Unbanz prepares the appeal.',
 'Ad account disabled for circumventing systems?', 'Circumventing systems',
 'The notice says your ad account was disabled for circumventing systems, and it rarely says why. This page is for advertisers who got that notice and want a clear appeal sent through Meta’s official review.',
 'Meta uses this notice when it believes an ad account is linked to one it already restricted, or that someone tried to get around its checks. You can request a review in Account Quality. Be honest about the history. A clean, specific appeal gives you the best chance, and Meta decides.',
 [('What it means', 'Meta thinks this account is connected to a restricted one through an admin, a card, a device, a domain or a business name.'),
  ('What to check', 'Look for shared admins, a payment card that sat on an old account, a login from the same device, or a domain used before.'),
  ('What not to do', 'Do not open a new ad account to keep running ads. That is the kind of behaviour the notice is about.')],
 [S('What the notice usually points to',
    'Meta does not tell you which link it found. In practice the trigger is one of a short list of things that tie two accounts together.',
    ul(['<strong>A person:</strong> the same admin profile, or someone who also manages an account that was disabled before.',
        '<strong>A payment method:</strong> a card or bank account that was used on a restricted ad account.',
        '<strong>A device or network:</strong> logins from the same computer or shared office connection.',
        '<strong>A business detail:</strong> the same business name, domain, pixel or Page as a restricted account.',
        '<strong>Behaviour:</strong> opening new accounts right after a restriction, or ads that change after approval.'])),
  S('What to do first',
    ol(['Open Account Quality and screenshot the notice and the date.',
        'Write down every account you or your team ran before this one, including ones that were restricted.',
        'Remove admins you do not recognise and turn on two-factor for everyone who stays.',
        'Stop running ads from any new account while the review is open.',
        'Request the review once and explain, in plain words, who you are, what you sell and how the accounts relate.'])),
  S('How to write the appeal',
    'Explain the connection if there is a real one. A shared card between two of your own businesses, or an agency that manages many clients, is common and can be explained. Hiding a link that Meta has already seen usually hurts you. Keep it short, factual and polite, and attach the proof that shows who runs the business.'),
  S('How Unbanz helps',
    'We read the notice, go through the account history with you and work out the most likely link. Then we write the appeal, gather the supporting details and send it through Meta’s official review. We do not use tricks, and we will tell you if we think an appeal has little chance. See also the guide on ' +
    A('/guides/ad-account-circumventing-systems/', 'circumventing systems') + ' and our page on ' + A('/can-i-make-a-new-ad-account-after-ban/', 'making a new ad account after a ban') + '.')],
 [('Can an ad account disabled for circumventing systems come back?', 'Sometimes. It depends on what Meta linked and whether the appeal explains it well. Meta makes the final decision and nobody can promise the result.'),
  ('Should I open a new ad account while I wait?', 'No. A new account tied to the same admin, card or domain can be disabled as well and can make the original harder to recover.'),
  ('Why does the notice not say what I did?', 'Meta keeps its detection methods private, so the notice stays general. We work from the account history to find the likely link.'),
  ('Does using a VPN cause this?', 'A VPN alone is not the usual reason, but logins from many countries can look unusual. Keep access consistent and tell Meta about remote team members.')],
 ['Advertisers whose notice mentions circumventing systems.', 'Businesses that ran an earlier ad account which was restricted.', 'Agencies and freelancers who manage several accounts from one login.'],
 send_extra=['A short list of earlier ad accounts, portfolios or Pages tied to this business.'])

page('ad-account-restricted-payment-issue', G,
 'Ad Account Restricted for a Payment Issue: What to Do',
 'Meta ad account restricted because of a payment issue? What the notice means, what to settle first and how Unbanz helps with the appeal.',
 'Ad account restricted because of a payment issue?', 'Payment issue restriction',
 'Meta restricts ad accounts when it cannot collect payment or does not trust a payment method. This page is for advertisers who see a payment-related notice and cannot run ads.',
 'A payment restriction usually means a failed charge, an unpaid balance or a card Meta does not trust. Settle what you owe, check the payment method in Billing, then request a review in Account Quality. If the button is missing or the review is denied, Unbanz can prepare the appeal.',
 [('Settle the balance', 'An unpaid amount blocks most reviews. Open Billing in Ads Manager and clear the outstanding charge first.'),
  ('Check the method', 'Expired cards, bank declines, a wrong billing address or a card used on many accounts can all trigger the notice.'),
  ('Then ask for review', 'Once billing is clean, request the review in Account Quality with a short, honest note.')],
 [S('What a payment restriction can look like',
    ul(['Ads stop and Ads Manager shows a payment failed or payment method needs attention message.',
        'A spending limit appears or drops, and you cannot raise it.',
        'The ad account shows as restricted or disabled with a billing reason.',
        'The Request review button is missing until the balance is paid.'])),
  S('Things to check in Billing',
    ol(['Open Billing and payments for the ad account and read every notice.',
        'Look at the payment activity for failed or pending charges and pay the outstanding amount.',
        'Make sure the card, its expiry date and the billing address are correct and the name matches the business.',
        'Ask your bank whether it declined or flagged the Meta charges, since banks sometimes block them.',
        'Remove old cards you no longer use, and add one clean method rather than several.'])),
  S('What makes it harder',
    'A card that was used on an ad account Meta restricted before, a charge that was disputed with the bank, or a card shared across many unrelated ad accounts can turn a billing problem into a wider restriction. In those situations the payment fix alone is not enough, and the appeal needs to explain the history.'),
  S('How Unbanz helps',
    'We go through the notice and your billing history, tell you what needs to be settled first, and then prepare the appeal and supporting details for Meta’s official review. We never take card numbers or logins. For the wider picture see ' +
    A('/guides/meta-ad-payment-declined-fix/', 'fixing a declined Meta ad payment') + ' and ' + A('/guides/meta-ad-account-disabled-payment/', 'ad accounts disabled for payment or unusual activity') + '.')],
 [('Why was my ad account restricted for payment reasons?', 'Common reasons are a failed charge, an unpaid balance, a card Meta does not trust, or a payment method tied to an account that was restricted before.'),
  ('Do I need to pay before I request a review?', 'Usually yes. An outstanding balance blocks most reviews, so clear it first and keep proof of payment.'),
  ('Will a new card fix the restriction?', 'Not on its own. A new card helps only if the old one was the problem. If Meta linked the account to another one, the appeal still has to explain that.'),
  ('Can Unbanz pay my Meta balance?', 'No. You pay Meta directly. Unbanz only prepares and sends the appeal.')],
 ['Advertisers with a failed charge or an unpaid balance.', 'Businesses whose card was declined and whose ad account is now restricted.', 'Agencies paying for several clients from one card.'],
 send_extra=['A screenshot of the billing page showing the amount due and the payment activity.'])

page('ad-account-disabled-after-adding-new-card', G,
 'Ad Account Disabled After Adding a New Card',
 'Ad account restricted or disabled right after you added a new card or changed payment details? Why it happens and how to request a review.',
 'Ad account disabled after adding a new card?', 'Disabled after a new card',
 'Changing a payment method is one of the moments Meta watches closely. This page is for advertisers whose ad account was restricted or disabled soon after adding or switching a card.',
 'A new card can trigger a restriction when Meta sees it as a change in who controls the account, or when the card is linked to a restricted account. Check the card details, remove any card you do not recognise, then request a review once. If it fails, Unbanz can prepare the appeal.',
 [('Why timing matters', 'Meta checks account changes, and a new card, new admin or new country together can look like a takeover.'),
  ('Check the card', 'Name, billing address and expiry must be correct. A prepaid or virtual card shared across accounts is often a problem.'),
  ('Check for a takeover', 'If you did not add the card, treat it as a hack. Secure the profile and remove the card before anything else.')],
 [S('Why a new card can trigger a restriction',
    ul(['The card was used on another ad account that Meta restricted or disabled.',
        'The same card is attached to many ad accounts that look unrelated.',
        'A virtual or prepaid card was declined, which counts as a failed charge.',
        'Someone else added the card after getting into an admin profile.',
        'The billing country on the card does not match the business country you set.'])),
  S('What to do',
    ol(['Open Billing and payments and see which card is attached and who added it.',
        'If you do not recognise it, remove it, change the admin passwords and turn on two-factor, then read our guide on ' + A('/ad-account-disabled-after-hack/', 'hacked ad accounts') + '.',
        'If it is yours, make sure the name and address match the business and the card is a normal debit or credit card.',
        'Clear any pending charge.',
        'Request a review in Account Quality and say plainly what you changed and why.'])),
  S('What to avoid',
    'Do not rotate through several new cards hoping one will work. Each failed attempt is another signal, and it can spread the restriction to more accounts. Do not send card details to anyone offering to help.'),
  S('How Unbanz helps',
    'We read the notice and the timeline, work out whether the card or something around it is the likely trigger, and prepare the appeal. We never need card numbers. You can compare notice types on our page on ' + A('/meta-ad-account-restricted-vs-disabled/', 'restricted versus disabled') + '.')],
 [('Can a new payment method get my ad account disabled?', 'It can. A card tied to a restricted account, or a change that looks like a takeover, can lead to a restriction.'),
  ('Should I remove the card?', 'If you did not add it, yes, and secure the profile first. If it is yours and correct, leave it and request a review.'),
  ('Does a virtual card cause problems?', 'Some virtual and prepaid cards are declined or shared across accounts, which Meta can treat as a risk. A standard card in the business name is safer.'),
  ('Will Unbanz ask for my card number?', 'No. We never need card numbers, passwords or codes.')],
 ['Advertisers who changed a card and lost access shortly after.', 'Businesses that suspect someone else added a payment method.', 'Teams that moved billing from one card to another.'],
 send_extra=['When you added or changed the card, and who did it.'])

page('ad-account-disabled-by-mistake', G,
 'Ad Account Disabled by Mistake? How to Appeal',
 'Think Meta disabled your ad account by mistake? What a wrong flag looks like, what proof helps and how Unbanz prepares the appeal.',
 'Ad account disabled by mistake?', 'Disabled by mistake',
 'Automated systems make errors, and plenty of honest advertisers get flagged. This page is for people who ran clean ads and cannot see what they did wrong.',
 'If your ad account was disabled and you cannot find a reason, start by confirming what Meta actually flagged in Account Quality. Then request a review with proof that you are a real business running allowed ads. A calm, specific appeal works better than a long complaint.',
 [('Confirm the flag', 'Account Quality shows what Meta flagged. Sometimes it is a single ad, your profile or the portfolio, not the whole business.'),
  ('Gather proof', 'Business registration, website, invoices and screenshots of your ads show you are what you say you are.'),
  ('Keep it short', 'One review request with clear facts. Long emotional messages and repeated requests do not help.')],
 [S('Signs it may be a wrong flag',
    ul(['The ads that ran were ordinary products or services with accurate claims.',
        'Nothing changed recently: same card, same admins, same landing page.',
        'There was no earlier rejection or warning in Account Quality.',
        'The notice is general and does not point to an ad or a policy.'])),
  S('Check before you argue',
    'Even when it feels like a mistake, look for the small things that tip automated checks. A landing page that is slow or broken, a missing privacy page, an ad that mentions a personal attribute, a profile that logged in from a new place, or a sudden jump in daily spend are common. Fix what you find, then say so in the appeal.'),
  S('What goes into a good appeal',
    ol(['Who you are: the business name, what you sell and where you operate.',
        'What you were advertising, with the ad and the landing page.',
        'What you believe was flagged, and what you checked or changed.',
        'Proof: registration, website, product photos, invoices.',
        'A request for a human to look again.'])),
  S('How Unbanz helps',
    'We read the notice and the account timeline with you, point out what could have triggered the flag, and write the appeal. Then we send it through Meta’s official review. If we think a review will not help, we say so before you pay. Related: ' +
    A('/why-was-my-facebook-ad-account-disabled-without-warning/', 'disabled without warning') + ' and ' + A('/ad-account-request-review-not-showing/', 'no request review button') + '.')],
 [('Can Meta disable an ad account by mistake?', 'Yes. Automated systems make wrong calls. A review by a person can change the outcome, though Meta makes the final decision.'),
  ('Why is there no reason in the notice?', 'Meta often keeps the wording general. Account Quality and the account history give better clues.'),
  ('Should I contact Meta support first?', 'If the support route is open to you, use it and keep the reply. If it is not, a formal review request in Account Quality is the main route.'),
  ('How many times should I appeal?', 'Once, done properly. Repeating the same request does not add anything and can slow things down.')],
 ['Honest advertisers who cannot see what went wrong.', 'Shops and service businesses with a clean ad history.', 'Teams whose ad account was disabled the same day they launched.'])

page('meta-business-portfolio-restricted-help', G,
 'Business Portfolio Restricted: Get Help With the Appeal',
 'Meta Business Portfolio restricted or disabled? What it affects, what to check first and how Unbanz helps you appeal through Meta’s official review.',
 'Business portfolio restricted?', 'Business portfolio restricted',
 'When a business portfolio (the old Business Manager) is restricted, every ad account, Page and pixel inside it can stop working. This page is for owners who see that notice and need to act in the right order.',
 'A restricted portfolio blocks advertising across everything inside it. Open Account Quality, select the portfolio itself, read the reason and request a review. Check business verification and admins first. If you cannot see a review button or it was denied, Unbanz can prepare the appeal.',
 [('Select the right asset', 'In Account Quality choose the portfolio, not only an ad account. The portfolio has its own status and review button.'),
  ('Check admins and verification', 'Unknown admins, a compromised profile or mismatched business documents are frequent causes.'),
  ('Do not start a new one', 'A second portfolio for the same business can be linked and restricted too, which makes recovery harder.')],
 [S('What a restricted portfolio affects',
    ul(['Every ad account and the campaigns running inside it.',
        'Pages, Instagram accounts and catalogs you manage through the portfolio.',
        'Pixels and data sources, which may stop collecting events for ads.',
        'Your ability to add people, assets or payment methods.'])),
  S('Why portfolios get restricted',
    ul(['An admin profile was hacked or restricted, and the problem spread to the portfolio.',
        'Repeated policy problems in one ad account.',
        'The portfolio is linked to another portfolio that was disabled.',
        'Business verification failed or the documents do not match what you entered.',
        'A payment problem that was not settled.'])),
  S('Steps in order',
    ol(['Screenshot the notice in Account Quality and write down the date.',
        'Check every person and partner with access and remove ones you do not know.',
        'Turn on two-factor for all admins and make sure at least two trusted people are admins.',
        'Check business verification: legal name, address and website must match your documents.',
        'Request the review for the portfolio once, with a short factual note.'])),
  S('How Unbanz helps',
    'We read the notice, go through the people and assets in the portfolio, and prepare the appeal and the supporting documents. It goes through Meta’s official review. Read more on ' +
    A('/business-manager-disabled/', 'Business Manager disabled') + ' and in the guide to ' + A('/guides/meta-business-portfolio-restricted/', 'requesting a portfolio review') + '.')],
 [('What is the difference between a restricted portfolio and a restricted ad account?', 'The portfolio holds your ad accounts, Pages and people. A portfolio restriction affects everything inside it. An ad account restriction affects that one account.'),
  ('Is Business Manager the same as a business portfolio?', 'Yes, Meta now calls it a business portfolio. People still say Business Manager.'),
  ('Can I move my ad account to a new portfolio?', 'Not as a way around a restriction. Meta can link the new portfolio to the old one, and the restriction can follow.'),
  ('Do I need business verification?', 'Not always, but Meta asks for it for some features and after some restrictions. Use the legal name and documents that match your registration.')],
 ['Business owners whose whole portfolio is restricted.', 'Agencies that manage client ad accounts in one portfolio.', 'Teams that lost admin access after a profile was disabled.'],
 send_extra=['A list of the admins on the portfolio and which of them you trust.'])

page('business-manager-restricted-cant-add-ad-account', G,
 'Business Manager Restricted: Cannot Add Ad Accounts',
 'Business Manager or portfolio restricted and you cannot create or add ad accounts? Why it happens and what you can try before asking for help.',
 'Business Manager restricted, cannot add ad accounts?', 'Cannot add ad accounts',
 'You open your business settings and the option to create or add an ad account is greyed out or fails. This page is for owners who hit that wall.',
 'When a portfolio is restricted, Meta often blocks creating or adding ad accounts. Check Account Quality for the portfolio status, look at your own profile and your role, and request a review for the portfolio. Do not try to work around it with another portfolio.',
 [('Check your role', 'You need admin access on the portfolio. A lost admin role looks like a restriction but is a different problem.'),
  ('Check the portfolio', 'A restricted portfolio can still show assets but will not let you add ad accounts.'),
  ('Check your profile', 'A restriction on your own profile can block you from creating anything in business settings.')],
 [S('Three different problems that look the same',
    ul(['<strong>You are not an admin.</strong> Ask a current admin to give you full control, or follow the lost admin steps in our guide to ' + A('/guides/meta-business-portfolio-lost-admin-access/', 'lost admin access') + '.',
        '<strong>Your personal profile is restricted.</strong> It may stop you creating ad accounts even though the portfolio is fine.',
        '<strong>The portfolio is restricted.</strong> Account Quality shows it and the review button sits on the portfolio.'])),
  S('Where Meta usually limits you',
    'Meta commonly limits the number of ad accounts a new or lightly used portfolio can create, until the business is verified or has a clean spending history. A message about reaching a limit is not the same as a restriction. A message that your portfolio is restricted or that you cannot create assets points to a review.'),
  S('What to try',
    ol(['Open Account Quality and select the portfolio. Note whether it says restricted, disabled or limited.',
        'Check the people list and your own role in business settings.',
        'Complete business verification if Meta offers it.',
        'Request a review for whichever asset is flagged, once.',
        'Wait for the answer before creating anything new.'])),
  S('How Unbanz helps',
    'We work out which of the three problems you have, then prepare the appeal for the portfolio or the profile. See also our page on ' + A('/meta-business-portfolio-restricted-help/', 'restricted business portfolios') + '.')],
 [('Why can I not create an ad account in Business Manager?', 'It can be a role problem, a limit on new portfolios, a restriction on your profile or a restriction on the portfolio. Account Quality shows which.'),
  ('Is there a limit on ad accounts per portfolio?', 'Yes, Meta limits how many a portfolio can hold, and the limit can be lower for newer or unverified portfolios.'),
  ('Can I just open a new portfolio?', 'It is risky. If Meta links it to the restricted one, the new portfolio can be restricted as well.'),
  ('Does business verification lift the limit?', 'It can raise some limits, but it does not remove a policy restriction.')],
 ['Owners who cannot add or create ad accounts.', 'Agencies adding client accounts to a portfolio.', 'Businesses with a new portfolio that hit a limit.'])
